@startuml agile_workflow_detailed
' SmartExam process model (Chapter-1-8, fig:agileworkflowdetailed): Scrum-style sprints as
' described in Chapter-1-8, Chapter-3-3 (definition of done, schedule control) and
' Chapter-3-5 (sprint meetings, written check-ins, 24-hour blocker rule, change control).
' Output name is agile_workflow_detailed.png (set by the @startuml name above).
' UML 2.5 activity diagram: partitions, initial/final nodes, fork/join, guarded decisions.
' Legibility: 13 pt text in a PNG about 1180 px wide prints at about 7 pt at 0.9\linewidth.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng agile_workflow.puml
!include style.iuml
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam note {
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam swimlane {
  TitleFontSize 13
  TitleFontStyle bold
  BorderColor #999999
}

|Development team (3 members)|
start
:Product backlog
(FR1-FR12, modules M1-M12);
repeat
  :Sprint planning: sprint goal and
  sprint backlog (each task has one
  WBS code and one owner);
  fork
    :Develop the module;
  fork again
    :Write its xUnit and
    Playwright tests;
  end fork
  note right
    4-week sprint:
    written check-ins;
    blocker unsolved
    for 24 h -> team
    discussion
  end note
  :Increment: tasks meet the definition
  of done (code and tests pass,
  thesis section updated);
  |Supervisor|
  :Sprint review: the increment is
  demonstrated; feedback on it and
  on the backlog priorities;
  |Development team (3 members)|
  :Schedule check: if under 80 % of
  story points are done, move or
  cut backlog items;
  :Feedback and accepted changes
  go into the product backlog;
repeat while (Sprint 8 finished?) is ([no: next sprint]) not ([yes])
:Integrated system, final
thesis and demo (Week 32);
stop
@enduml
